course: dictionary
lesson: 2624
title: One word, two sounds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are spelled the same but are said differently and mean different things. Desert is one. As a noun, it is said «DEZ-ert» and means a large area of land. As a verb, it is said «di-ZURT» and means to leave someone and not come back. Context tells you which one you need.
explain: Look at this: «Nobody should desert a friend who needs help.» Desert is a verb here, and the stress is on the second part. It means to leave when you should stay. Try the meaning in the sentence: «Nobody should leave a friend who needs help.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Now look at this: «The desert fennec fox has huge ears that give off heat to keep it cool.» Desert is a noun here, a place. The clues are fox, heat and cool, which all fit a hot, dry place with very little rain.
explain: A deserted place is different again. «A deserted street» has nobody in it. Deserted is the word for an empty place, so the sound and the meaning both come from the verb's past form.
fact: A desert is a large area of land that gets very little rain, so few plants grow there.
fact: Deserts can be sandy, rocky, hot or cold. Antarctica is the largest desert, and it is a cold desert.
fact: Desert plants like cacti store water. Camels and lizards are animals that are suited to heat and little water.
fact: Deserts are hot by day and can be cold at night, so carry water and sun protection.
fact: The Sahara in Africa, the Mojave in the USA and the Great Victoria Desert in Australia are all deserts.
exercise: In «Cacti grow in the desert», what is the desert? | *A large area of land with very little rain | A large building full of cats | A wet valley with many rivers | A town with nobody in it
exercise: Ayla says, «Would a good friend desert you when you need help?» What does desert mean here, said «di-ZURT»? | To build a sandy hill | *To leave someone and not come back when you should stay | To sleep under the stars | To find a lost map
exercise: «The deserted street was silent at midnight.» What does deserted mean? | *With nobody in it | Very hot and sunny | Full of cars and people | Covered in snow
test: Which animal gets almost all its water from its food, as in «Many desert animals, like hopping mice»? | Lamb in a spring field | *Hopping mouse | Blackberry bush | Fire ant
test: How is desert said when it is a noun, as in «the desert fennec fox»? | di-ZURT | DEE-zert | dez-ERT | *DEZ-ert
exam: In «Water even moves across a desert», what does desert mean? | To leave a place for ever | A quiet, empty room | *A large area of land with very little rain | A small pond full of fish
